Based on the scene described and the ontology provided, here is the semantic interpretation grounded in the fixed OWL ontology vocabulary.

Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "Unusual Weather Condition with Obstacle" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :StateAnomaly ;
    :hasActor :actor1 ;
    :hasActor :actor2 ;
    :hasObstacle :obstacle1 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk2 .

:actor1 a :Cyclist .
:actor2 a :Cyclist .

:obstacle1 a :RoadObject .

:weather1 a :RainyCondition .

:risk1 a :PedestrianCollisionRisk ;
    :description "Risk of collision with cyclist due to visibility reduction." ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :DistractionRisk ;
    :description "Distraction caused by unusual large elephant statues." ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.60"^^xsd:float .
```

